<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- UMW_Pointed. Point shape — a fine needle that slips past armor and bone to find the organs.
       IDENTITY: the trait's lever is WHERE the wound lands, not how big it is — a
       MeleeDamageConversionExtension reroutes the base Stab hit to UMW_Stab_Deep, raising
       stabChanceOfForcedInternal 0.6 -> 0.85 (the def carries the worked mechanics and sizing).
       Keep it OFF the damage-vs-AP axis: the roster already leans on factor tradeoffs there
       (HeadWeighted, Counterweighted, Studded, Razored), so a stat-shaped NeedlePoint is a me-too.
       Organ-seeking is an untouched axis, is literally the "drives deeper" fiction, and
       differentiates the Point family: raw armor answer (ArmorSpike), attrition bleeding (Barbed),
       vitals-seeking lethality (this) — the kill-weapon mirror of Opiated's capture coating.
       Conversion and tool mods alike touch only Stab-capacity swings, so the spear and knife are its
       prime carriers; a longsword or gladius is affected only on point-tool swings.

       DAMAGE/AP are UNCOUPLED and Stab-only, via MeleeToolModExtension — NOT a weapon-wide
       MeleeWeapon_DamageMultiplier rider, which would buff a longsword's edge cuts too, which a
       point trait has no business doing.
       - armorPenetrationFactor x1.3 = PiercingArrows, Odyssey's "bodkin-tipped arrows" — its own
         needle-point fiction and the named anchor. A FACTOR, not a floor, on purpose: the floor is
         ArmorSpike's identity (a guaranteed baseline that rescues poor quality/soft stuff), while a
         factor sharpens what quality provides (masterwork plasteel spear ~0.84, earned, vs the
         knife's honest 0.26).
       - damageFactor x0.95: a needle cuts a narrow channel (cf. Counterweighted's x0.95 coupled
         cost); also the governor on the lethality stack, since a forced-internal strike already
         delivers 115% of rolled damage split 75% outer / 40% organ.

       VEHICLE for the malus: weapon-wide MeleeWeapon_CooldownMultiplier statFactor —
       vanilla-applied (CompUniqueWeapon.GetStatFactor), vanilla-displayed, consumed per swing by
       Tool.AdjustedCooldown. This REPLACED an equippedStatOffsets MeleeHitChance -1 wielder malus
       (v1.0.x): that field is bladelink-only in vanilla, and the Harmony patch that routed it live
       rode vanilla's stat pipeline tens of thousands of times per frame as this trait's sole
       consumer. A cooldown factor prices the same "hard to place cleanly" fiction as weapon
       handling instead of wielder skill, matching how Odyssey expresses every one of its maluses
       (weapon-thing stats, never wielder-side). Weapon-wide is accepted, unlike the per-tool
       damage/AP mods below: there is no per-tool cooldown stat (Tool.AdjustedCooldown = tool base x
       this one factor), and a deliberate weapon reads fine slowing a spear's pole strike too.

       TUNING: x1.05 cooldown = x0.952 throughput, flat across skill. The old -1 raw MeleeHitChance
       cost ~4% relative hit rate at the mid-skill knot and ~1% at raw 20; x1.05 sits at the
       mid-skill equivalence and no longer fades for masters — acceptably close, and it keeps the
       identity math: raw Stab DPS still nets slightly NEGATIVE (x0.95 damage / x1.05 cooldown ≈
       x0.905, ~-9.5% before armor, vs ~-9% before) — deliberate and honest: the payoff is
       placement (85% organ strikes) and penetration (x1.3), not throughput. cf. FrequencyAmplifier,
       Odyssey's cooldown-priced coupled cost (x1.5 there, on a far larger buff).
       MV 70: PiercingArrows prices the +30% AP alone at 40; the organ-seeking premium sits it
       below ParalyticArrows' 80 / HollowPoint's 85, discounted for the cooldown and damage
       costs. -->
  <WeaponTraitDef>
    <defName>UMW_NeedlePoint</defName>
    <label>needle point</label>
    <description>Tapered to a fine needle, the point drives deep beneath bone and muscle, seeking the organs within. Placing it cleanly demands slower, deliberate thrusts.</description>
    <commonality>1</commonality>
    <weaponCategory>UMW_Pointed</weaponCategory>
    <exclusionTags>
      <li>Point</li>
    </exclusionTags>
    <statOffsets>
      <MarketValue>70</MarketValue> <!-- PiercingArrows 40 prices the AP; organ premium below ParalyticArrows 80; see header -->
    </statOffsets>
    <statFactors>
      <MeleeWeapon_CooldownMultiplier>1.05</MeleeWeapon_CooldownMultiplier> <!-- x0.952 throughput, ~= the old -1 MeleeHitChance at mid skill; see header -->
    </statFactors>
    <traitAdjectives>
      <li>needle</li>
      <li>needling</li>
      <li>hypodermic</li>
    </traitAdjectives>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="UniqueMeleeWeapons.MeleeDamageConversionExtension">
        <conversions>
          <li>
            <from>Stab</from>
            <to>UMW_Stab_Deep</to>
          </li>
        </conversions>
      </li>
      <li Class="UniqueMeleeWeapons.MeleeToolModExtension">
        <mods>
          <li>
            <capacities>
              <li>Stab</li>
            </capacities>
            <damageFactor>0.95</damageFactor>
            <armorPenetrationFactor>1.3</armorPenetrationFactor> <!-- cf. PiercingArrows +30% -->
          </li>
        </mods>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </WeaponTraitDef>

</Defs>
